# CP13.2 — correct the timing figures, split the two hypotheses.
#
# F22. The two timing hypotheses are separated everywhere. They came apart and
#      were reported as one finding, which understated recency and overstated
#      liquidity. Liquidity is withdrawn; recency survived. A83's withdrawal
#      stands and its scope is unchanged.
#
# F23. SF-2's attribution stated next to the number, and decomposed. The bare
#      count conflates "rarely in a position to make the mistake" with
#      "disciplined about not making it".
#
# F24. The 2k/10k divergence recorded, including that a per-class figure at
#      2,000 cases is not stable.
#
# F25. §19 rewritten once and frozen at nine.

README.md
KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md
out/model_report.json
